      <slug></slug>
      <title>OpenSound System v4 port to Haiku</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Alt-OS</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;OpenSound System (OSS) is the first attempt in unifying the digital audio architecture for UNIX. OSS is a set of device drivers that provide a uniform API across all the major UNIX architectures, released under BSD/GPL licences.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will describe the required steps for the port of OpenSound System v4 to the Haiku operating system.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="121">François Revol</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>